+		 * translation unit does not get kern_exec.o's CFLAGS and MAXCOMLEN is
+		 * not guaranteed visible here.  p_comm is char[MAXCOMLEN+1], so
+		 * sizeof is the right bound and needs no macro.
+		 *
+		 * GUARDED ON XNU_NATIVE_VIRTIO_CONSOLE, which
+		 * build-xnu-4k-baseline.sh now passes to kern_exit.o for exactly this.
+		 * Not XNU_OWNER_CACHE_MOUNT: that macro is kern_exec.o's, so the
+		 * emitter would compile out here and the boot would be silent about
+		 * exits for a reason no compiler reports.  The exec record keeps its
+		 * own guard; the two halves of the pair sit in different translation
+		 * units and each needs the macro its own object is actually given.
+		 *
+		 * AND THE LITERAL WILL NOT BE GREPPABLE IN THE IMAGE, which is
+		 * measured and not guessed: ld's SHF_MERGE|SHF_STRINGS pass split the
+		 * exec record's 30-byte literal into a 16-byte head plus a shared
+		 * tail, so exec.seen counts ZERO as a contiguous byte string in the
+		 * kernel that carries it.  The record arrives on the wire complete.
+		 * The block-scope static is what proves the code is there.
